94139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543964 1083 #uuid "02b9cb0a-4110-548b-9b97-4a59eda21d43" 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543965 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544000 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543965 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543965 1071 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by the closed curve $C$ with positive orientation and parametrization $r(t)=\\langle 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}, 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}, 1\\rangle$ for $t\\in [0,2 \\pi).$\nGiven that $F(x,y,z)=\\langle y, - x, 0\\rangle,$ evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_S\\operatorname{curl}F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}S.\n$$" 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543965 1072 #uuid "07a605d5-0ef0-5420-9db8-ccb3e82bd11b" 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543965 1074 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by a simple, closed, piecewise-smooth boundary $C$ with positive orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $S,$ then Stokes' theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad z=1\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\langle y, - x, 0\\rangle \\\\ & =\\langle \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right), - \\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right), 0\\rangle \\\\ & =\\langle 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}, - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}, 0\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r\\prime(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\prime(t) & =\\langle \\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right), \\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right), \\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(1\\right)\\rangle \\\\ & =\\langle - 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}, 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}, 0\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r\\prime(t) & =\\langle 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}, - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}, 0\\rangle\\cdot \\langle - 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}, 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}, 0\\rangle \\\\ & =\\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(- 6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(- 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\ & =- 6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S\\operatorname{curl}F\\cdot\\mathrm dS & =\\oint_C F\\cdot\\mathrm dr \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi} F(r(t))\\cdot r\\prime(t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\left(-6\\right)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ & =\\left[\\left(- 6 t\\right)\\right]_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ & =\\left(\\left(- 12 \\pi\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(0\\right)\\right) \\\\ & =- 12 \\pi\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543966 1080 "12" 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543966 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543966 1083 #uuid "1a586ec0-0624-5fa5-bb42-b553aa1955f5" 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543967 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543982 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543967 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543967 1071 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by the closed curve $C$ with positive orientation and parametrization $r(t)=\\langle 4 t^{3} - 4 t, 9 t^{2} + 9 t, 3 t^{3} - 3 t\\rangle$ for $t\\in [-1,0).$\nGiven that $F(x,y,z)=\\langle - z, 0, - y\\rangle,$ evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_S\\operatorname{curl}F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}S.\n$$" 13194139535933 17592186045443 true] [17592186543967